      "id": "expand-and-cancel",
      "title": "Expand and cancel matching terms",
      "explanation": "Splitting the factors into round-number parts reveals matching terms in the two products. By the distributive property,\n\\[\n9901\\cdot101=(9900+1)(100+1)=990000+9900+100+1,\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n99\\cdot10101=99(10000+100+1)=990000+9900+99.\n\\]\nSubtracting cancels the common terms \\(990000+9900\\), leaving\n\\[\n100+1-99=2.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{2}\\), choice \\(\\text{A}\\).",
      "directNodeIds": [
        "cnm_p116"
      ],
      "sourceRef": "amc/2024_AMC_10A_Q01#expand-and-cancel"
    }
